 ### Read the result
 
 On the routes checked, the columns were Main (standard seat), EvenMore (extra legroom), and Mint (lie-flat, on some routes);
- take the names from the header. Each cell shows the cheapest fare in its column. Clicking a cell opens tier cards, which this search does not open;
- the Main column opened Main Base, Main, and Main Flex. Prices are one-way per person, round trips included. Round trip pages show outbound rows first;
- return rows render only after an outbound is picked, which this search must not do.
+ United-operated rows show Economy and Business/First prices instead. Each cell shows the cheapest tier in its column. Its tier cards, for Main: Main Base, Main, and Main Flex, give each tier's price, carry-on, seat choice, and change and cancel terms. Prices are one-way per person with taxes and fees, round trips included. A strip above the rows gives each nearby day's lowest fare.
 
